  "body": "Every circle and fillet posts as G01 chords: the 602-line EDM-T2 Sodick program has no G02/G03; the dia-8 hole is about 60 segments (about 5 um chord error, above wire finishing tolerance). Wire controls and the owner's programs use arcs.\n\nDone means: wire paths keep true arcs from the model through to G02/G03 in the Sodick and wire-iso posts (a full circle and a fillet pinned by goldens); chords remain only for true splines.\n\nFound in a wire EDM validation run of CamCraft 0.24.0 through the camcraft MCP (2026-11-21), on test parts in `~/Desktop/camcraft/edm-validation/` (EDM-T1 square, EDM-T2 2-axis block, EDM-T3 taper block) and a Sodick owner's own UV part (#617). Wire EDM-W025 (0.25 mm), Sodick ALC400G with test conditions.",
